<slide id="trust_controls">
  <background color="paper"/>
  <shape id="workflow-line" type="rect" x="48" y="40" width="4" height="620" fill="hairline"/>
  <text id="title" x="86" y="52" width="760" height="46" font="heading" size="30" color="ink" wrap="false">Trust and integrity by design</text>
  <text id="subtitle" x="86" y="102" width="1060" height="48" font="body" size="20" color="muted" line-height="1.3"><p>The platform is designed so that speed does not come at the cost of accountability, evidence integrity, or public confidence.</p></text>

  <shape id="card-1" type="rect" x="86" y="186" width="332" height="170" fill="surface" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <icon id="icon-1" name="file-signature" x="112" y="214" width="28" height="28" color="primary"/>
  <text id="title-1" x="152" y="212" width="220" height="24" font="body" size="20" color="ink" wrap="false"><strong>Signed audit packages</strong></text>
  <text id="body-1" x="112" y="256" width="270" height="70" font="body" size="17" color="muted" line-height="1.35"><p>Exported audit logs carry tamper-evident metadata that helps prove integrity after they leave the platform.</p></text>

  <shape id="card-2" type="rect" x="474" y="186" width="332" height="170" fill="surface" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <icon id="icon-2" name="key-round" x="500" y="214" width="28" height="28" color="accent"/>
  <text id="title-2" x="540" y="212" width="220" height="24" font="body" size="20" color="ink" wrap="false"><strong>Public-key verification</strong></text>
  <text id="body-2" x="500" y="256" width="270" height="70" font="body" size="17" color="muted" line-height="1.35"><p>External parties can independently validate signed audit packages against published verification details.</p></text>

  <shape id="card-3" type="rect" x="862" y="186" width="332" height="170" fill="surface" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <icon id="icon-3" name="route" x="888" y="214" width="28" height="28" color="#B45309"/>
  <text id="title-3" x="928" y="212" width="220" height="24" font="body" size="20" color="ink" wrap="false"><strong>Chain of custody</strong></text>
  <text id="body-3" x="888" y="256" width="270" height="70" font="body" size="17" color="muted" line-height="1.35"><p>The platform records who handled evidence and audit packages, when they did so, and what changed.</p></text>

  <shape id="card-4" type="rect" x="86" y="400" width="332" height="170" fill="surface" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <icon id="icon-4" name="shield-ellipsis" x="112" y="428" width="28" height="28" color="primary"/>
  <text id="title-4" x="152" y="426" width="220" height="24" font="body" size="20" color="ink" wrap="false"><strong>Supervisor controls</strong></text>
  <text id="body-4" x="112" y="470" width="270" height="70" font="body" size="17" color="muted" line-height="1.35"><p>Overrides and reassignments are allowed for exceptions, but they remain permanently visible in the audit trail.</p></text>

  <shape id="card-5" type="rect" x="474" y="400" width="332" height="170" fill="surface" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <icon id="icon-5" name="wifi-off" x="500" y="428" width="28" height="28" color="accent"/>
  <text id="title-5" x="540" y="426" width="220" height="24" font="body" size="20" color="ink" wrap="false"><strong>Offline field continuity</strong></text>
  <text id="body-5" x="500" y="470" width="270" height="70" font="body" size="17" color="muted" line-height="1.35"><p>Inspectors can keep working with cached materials even when field connectivity is unreliable.</p></text>

  <shape id="card-6" type="rect" x="862" y="400" width="332" height="170" fill="surface" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <icon id="icon-6" name="fingerprint" x="888" y="428" width="28" height="28" color="#B45309"/>
  <text id="title-6" x="928" y="426" width="220" height="24" font="body" size="20" color="ink" wrap="false"><strong>Protected local access</strong></text>
  <text id="body-6" x="888" y="470" width="270" height="70" font="body" size="17" color="muted" line-height="1.35"><p>Encrypted local cache and biometric unlock protect sensitive audit materials carried by field teams.</p></text>

  <text id="footer" x="70" y="684" width="520" height="18" font="caption" size="14" color="muted" wrap="false">IDLR-PTS Platform | Stakeholder PowerPoint deck</text>
